{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389092-how-to-build-awesome-brujah-paladin-like-in-dark-ages-first-edition-v20","id":1389092,"title":"How to build awesome Brujah (Paladin like) in Dark Ages (First Edition/V20)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-16T15:58:25-07:00","id":1389092,"title":"How to build awesome Brujah (Paladin like) in Dark Ages (First Edition/V20)?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> So I was thinking about creating sort of &quot;Holy Warrior Vampire&quot; in Dark Ages. Brujah came into my mind. How do you even build Brujah to be awesome? I consider one bonus Discipline to start with and I am thinking either Dominate, Fortitude, Auspex or Protean.<br /> <br /> Dominate because my character already will have quite strong social side + merits like Ability Aptitide (Intimidation, Empathy) + Enchanting Voice + Powerful Gaze. So since I want nice balance between combat and social abilities/powers - Dominate came to my mind.<br /> <br /> Fortitude - since we use First Edition rules for it- it soaks everything (including agg. damage) with Stamina by default, so I think it can work well with Potence + Celerity.<br /> <br /> Protean - well, who doesnt want Prot 2 for claws... But we have combo disciplines so I can always take V20 Burning Wrath (version which 1 BP - lasts whole scene) and combine it with Good Right/Left Hook merit for +2 damage with brawl attacks (not working for claws or castets). So it would deal then same damage as Claws and be more &quot;thematic&quot; for Brujah.<br /> <br /> Auspex - well, one of worst things that can happen is being jumped on by someone with Obfuscate so Auspex is good counter to it. I am not sure though if it's worth over Dominate or Fortitude for such combat-social character.<br /> <br /> As for my battle prowness I was thinking about using clan weakness for Frenzy and make it into weapon + couple other things.<br /> <br /> 1. Burning Wrath (version from Lore of Clans)<br /> 2. Ability Aptitide: Melee, Brawl, Dodge<br /> 3. Using Potence with Grapple manover to restrain target and use Bite to damage them. Since Potence gives auto-sucesses it should be powerful combo in 1v1.<br /> 4. Berserker merit + Fury\u2019s Focus - I can control my Frenzy and not attack people I don't want to. Which goes well with Berserker adding me +4 rolls to any combat rolls.<br /> 5. Cathartic Fury - I can regain Willpower points after Frenzy - each success - one willpower point. Which goes well with above 2 merits.<br /> <br /> What I have in mind is Warrior of God with Righteous Fury within Him who when taken to the edge - can release his Fury (Burning Wrath + Berserker) and deal with his enemies with his bare hands. When not he is very Charismatic person who tries to resolve conficts using his social charm + Presence discipline (and maybe Dominate).<br /> <br /> What do you think? Can I improve it more?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24341-viben","name":"Viben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T01:41:43-07:00","id":1389223,"title":"","content":"In my imagination, feral claws aren't needed for an iconic Paladin type character. A Brujah with Potence, Celerity, and a good melee weapon would do fine without it. <br /> <br /> I would suggest at least one dot in Animalism and some points in Animal Ken and Ride if you want to go the cavalier route and fight from horseback, though. Horsemanship remained a part of the traditional &quot;knight in shining armor&quot; fantasy even after the arrival of the musket made metal armor obsolete. <br /> <br /> A ghouled horse might even be worth a point in Allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T12:30:48-07:00","id":1389416,"title":"","content":"You could try looking at the Grail Knights from 'Ashen Knight' for Dark Ages Vampire. It's more 'Crusader' than Paladin but with some tweaking (borrow from other elements in some fashion like the Warrior Salubri) you could probably get something Paladin-esque. <br /> <br /> Of course this depends on what kind of 'Paladin' archetype you're thinking too, since there are alot of fictional paladin types through the decades I can think of. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:04:11-07:00","id":1389426,"title":"","content":"You don't need fortitude all that much if you're planning on wearing armour and you already have the other two physical disciplines (You should be killing enemies in a single blow and not be getting hit, and you're <i>extremely </i>mobile with Potence+celerity so running away is a non issue for you. <br /> <br /> Auspex is God's discipline. Playing without auspex makes me uncomfortable. <br /> Dominate... I love Dominate. I also really love DnD 5e's conquest paladin so it has a good amount of appeal. But traditional paladin wise, wining over hearts and minds/using your natural talents is more desirable than <i>programming </i>people to do what you want. Dominate is for smart manipulators and if you're playing knight in shining armour... Presence will do you just fine, Dominate is overkill. <br /> <br /> If you're wondering around a lot, meld earth is great, eyes of the beast is great but... GettiGng a third level out-of-clan utility discipline is not a magnificent investment. <br /> <br /> Of the disciplines you've suggested. I'd put auspex at 1, dominate at 2, protean at 3, fortitude at 4. If you can, pick the latter disciplines up later. I would actually suggest the following to you; Consider the other disciplines. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate; If we use a little historical realism, armour isn't really that bad for stealth. The real problem with armour is that it draws a lot of attention; Wearing a gambeson and having a sword on your hip is normal, wearing expensive mail and having a spear in hand is expecting trouble.If you use obfuscate, you can swagger around town in full plate holding the meatiest poleaxe you can find with nobody batting an eye. <br /> <br /> Animalsim: It's just really good during this time period. People are relying on animals so much more. <br /> <br /> and lastly<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy. <br /> I'm not asking you to be casting fireball (Though you can do it and yell &quot;SMITE EVIL&quot; if you really want to) but there are paths that would be of interest to a 'paladin' and above all, there are the rituals. Burning blade, Wards, Clinging of the insect, Wards, That one that makes the party invisible, Did I mention wards? Deliver righteous justice to some evil tremere and then<i> acquire</i> all their books, or work for the tremere in exchange for tutalage... <br /> <br /> The only problem with thaumaturgy is that you'll want to put points into Intelligence, and we both know if you want to be an Archtypical paladin that needs to be your dump stat so you can divest your three mentals into wits and/or perception. My recommendation would be to make socials your tertiary but then put all points into charisma; Give yourself some gnarly scars or otherwise uber-masculine your looks to thug levels to make yourself feel good about that 1 dot in appearance. <br /> <br /> Best advice would be to check what your party's packing and bring what they don't. But failing that. <br /> <br /> S tier: <br /> Auspex, Thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> A tier: <br /> Obfuscate, Animalism. <br /> <br /> B tier: <br /> Dominate,<br /> <br /> C tier<br /> Fortitude, Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T05:16:23-07:00","id":1390753,"title":"","content":"If you can get permission form the Storyteller, make a character who was alive during Charlemagne's reing and was an <i>actual</i> paladin. Or maybe someone who was a paladin, got Embraced, ended up in Torpor rather early, and only recently woke up, putting your age on par with other neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T21:37:04-07:00","id":1390915,"title":"","content":"A Salubri warrior might be more paladin like, at least D&amp;D style paladin. For a Brujah, as was mentioned you probably don't need the claws from Protean 2, especially if you're going to pick up burning wrath. I'm guessing you're planning on going with the road of kings for the whole chivalry angle? For a Brujah, eventually getting Presence up to 3 would be handy to entrance people, probably making Dominate not worth it at that point or much lower priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}